<p>Specify the tab configuration.</p>
<p>Available functions differ depending on the printer or printer driver 
 you are using.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="tab" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Default Tab:</span></p>
<p>Select the default tab which is displayed when you open a Printing Preferences 
 screen.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="menu" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Default Menu for Detailed Settings:</span></p>
<p>Select the default menu which is displayed when you open the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed 
 Settings</span> tab.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="type" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">One Click Preset List Type:</span></p>
<p>Specify a view style when you open the <span class="Term-Soft">Frequently 
 Used Settings</span> tab.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="property" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Printer Properties</span></p>
<p>Opens the printer properties dialog box.<br/>
You can configure the options installed on the printer or manage one click 
 presets on the <span class="Term-Soft">Accessories</span> and <span class="Term-Soft">Advanced 
 Options</span> tabs of the printer properties dialog box.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="about" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">About</span></p>
<p>Provides copyright and version information.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="diagnose" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Printer Diagnostic Correction Tool</span></p>
<p>If the printer does not print, click this button to start the tool to diagnose and fix the problem.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="wim" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Web Image Monitor...</span></p>
<p>Starts <span class="Term-Soft">Web Image Monitor</span>.</p>
<p>Web Image Monitor allows you to check the printer's status, manage jobs, 
 and change settings, via a Web browser. For details, see the <span class="Term-Soft">Web 
 Image Monitor</span> Help.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>This function is available only if your computer 
 is connected to the printer by the standard TCP/IP (IPv4/IPv6), WSD (IPv4), 
 IPP (IPv4), or Ridoc IO Navi (IPv4/IPv6/IPP) port.<br/>
 This function will be unavailable if the IPv6 address you specify includes 
 a number following the % symbol at the end of the address (also known 
 as the "zone identifier" or "scope ID"), or if your 
 computer is connected to this machine through network printer sharing.</p></li>
</ul>
